1 |   `F(w) ≥ 0`.  This is the key algebraic ingredient for the interface Boltzmann\n272 |   factor decomposition: after expanding the product of plaquette factors\n273 |   (product of sums = sum of products), each term is a product of characters\n274 |   grouped by link, and this lemma shows each such term has a separable character\n275 |   decomposition with non-negative coefficients.  0 sorries, 0 custom axioms\n276 |   beyond Peter–Weyl.  Verified by `#print axioms` (only `propext`,\n277 |   `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n278 | - `charProduct_mixed_finset_decomp'` (`PeterWeyl.lean`) — mixed-conjugation CG\n279 |   decomposition: a product of characters with mixed conjugation (some `χ(g)`,\n280 |   some `conj(χ(g))`) of the same group element decomposes as a non-negative-\n281 |   weighted sum of single characters `∑_w coeff w · χ_w(g)` with `coeff w ≥ 0`.\n282 |   The dual map converts `conj(χ)` to `χ_{dual}`, allowing `charProduct_finset_decomp'`\n283 |   to combine them.  This is the key lemma for the interface Boltzmann factor\n284 |   decomposition with inverted links.  0 sorries, 0 custom axioms beyond Peter–Weyl.\n285 |   Verified by `#print axioms` (only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n286 | - `charProduct_mixed_link_separable_decomp` (`PeterWeyl.lean`) — per-term\n287 |   separable decomposition with mixed conjugation: a product of characters (some\n288 |   conjugated, some not) grouped by link decomposes as a non-negative-weighted sum\n289 |   of products of single (unconjugated) characters `∑_w F(w) · ∏_l χ_{w(l)}(g_l)`\n290 |   with `F(w) ≥ 0`.  This is the key algebraic ingredient for the interface\n291 |   Boltzmann factor decomposition with inverted links: after expanding the\n292 |   product of plaquette factors, each term is a product of characters (some\n293 |   conjugated from inverted links) grouped by link, and this lemma shows each\n294 |   such term has a separable character decomposition with non-negative\n295 |   coefficients, with all conjugation resolved via the dual map.  0 sorries,\n296 |   0 custom axioms beyond Peter–Weyl.  Verified by `#print axioms` (only\n297 |   `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n298 |   `LinkVariable (SU N) Λ`, via `plaquetteContributionPD` (each plaquette\n299 |   factor PD by `comp_hom` from `plaquetteBoltzmannPD_inv`) and\n300 |   `PositiveDefinite.finprod` (n-ary Schur product).  0 sorries, 0 axioms\n301 |   beyond Peter–Weyl.\n302 | - `osG_thetaG_factorization` (`ReflectionPositivity.lean`) — the clean\n303 |   algebraic identity `osG(U)·osG(θU) = f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β S_W(U))`, showing\n304 |   `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` is equivalent to\n305 |   `∫ f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β S_W) dμ ≥ 0`.  0 sorries, 0 axioms.\n306 | - `PositiveDefinite.integral` (`PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean`) — the\n307 |   *continuous* analogue of `PositiveDefinite.sum`: an integral average of\n308 |   positive-definite functions is positive-definite.  Verified by\n309 |   `#print axioms` to depend on no custom axiom (only `propext`,\n310 |   `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`), 0 sorries.  This closes the \"integrate out\n311 |   interior links ⟹ the resulting kernel is PD\" step of the transfer-matrix\n312 |   positivity argument.\n313 | - `PositiveDefinite.integralOperator_nonneg` (`PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean`)\n314 |   — for a compact group `G` with probability measure `μ`, a continuous PD\n315 |   function `φ`, and a continuous `f`, `∫∫ f(x)·conj(f(y))·φ(x⁻¹y) dμ dμ ≥ 0`.\n316 |   The proof approximates the integral by Riemann sums (each non-negative by\n317 |   `PositiveDefinite.sum_nonneg_of_map`) and controls the error via uniform\n318 |   continuity on `G × G`.  Verified by `#print axioms` to depend on no custom\n319 |   axiom, 0 sorries.  This closes the \"PD kernel ⟹ positive integral operator\"\n320 |   step.  Together with `PositiveDefinite.integral`, both abstract sub-steps of\n321 |   the transfer-matrix positivity chain are now proved; the remaining work is\n322 |   the concrete wiring into the lattice-gauge-theory setup.\n323 | - `PositiveDefiniteKernel` (`PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean`) — Mercer-type\n324 |   PD kernel (no group structure needed): `K : X → X → ℂ` with\n325 |   `∑ c_i ·conj(c_j)·K(x_i, x_j) ≥ 0` for every finite set and coefficients.\n326 |   Building blocks (all 0 sorries, 0 axioms): `PositiveDefiniteKernel.conj_symm`\n327 |   (Hermitian symmetry), `.one` (constant-one kernel), `.mul` (Schur/Hadamard\n328 |   product theorem), `.smul_nonneg`, `.finprod` (n-ary Schur product), `.comp`\n329 |   (PD preserved by composition with `f : X → Y`), `.continuous_comp`\n330 |   (continuity preserved by composition), `.sum_nonneg_of_map` (non-injective\n331 |   index map), and `PositiveDefinite.toPositiveDefiniteKernel` (group-PD →\n332 |   Mercer-PD).\n333 | - `PositiveDefiniteKernel.integralOperator_nonneg`\n334 |   (`PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean`) — the Mercer-type generalization: a\n335 |   continuous Mercer-PD kernel on a compact space (no group structure needed)\n336 |   defines a positive integral operator\n337 |   `∫∫ f(x)·conj(f(y))·K(x, y) dμ dμ ≥ 0`.  0 sorries, 0 custom axioms.\n338 | - `character_expansion_positivity` and `character_expansion_nonneg`\n339 |   (`PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean`) — the **abstract character-expansion\n340 |   scaffold** for the reflection-positivity argument.  If a kernel\n341 |   `K : X → Y → ℂ` has a finite separable decomposition\n342 |   `K(x, y) = ∑_i a_i · Φ_i(x) · conj(Φ_i(θ y))` with `θ` measure-preserving\n343 |   (`θ_*ν = μ`), then for real-valued `f`:\n344 |   `∫∫ f(x)·f(θ y)·K(x, y) dν dμ = ∑_i a_i · ‖∫ f·Φ_i dμ‖²` (the identity), and\n345 |   with `a_i ≥ 0` this is non-negative (the corollary).  No group structure, no\n346 |   character orthogonality — only the measure-preserving change of variables and\n347 |   `f` real-valued.  This is the abstract scaffold that the concrete Peter–Weyl\n348 |   character expansion of the transfer-matrix kernel would plug into; it does\n349 |   **not** close `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` (which requires showing the TM\n350 |   kernel has the required separable decomposition — the Clebsch–Gordan gap).\n351 |   Verified by `#print axioms` (only `propext`, `Classical.choice`,\n352 |   `Quot.sound`), 0 sorries, 0 custom axioms.\n353 | \n354 | **Two independent verification checks were performed on both lemmas:**\n355 | 1. **`#print axioms`** — confirms no hidden axiom or `sorry` in the dependency\n356 |    tree (only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).  This catches\n357 |    *undeclared assumptions* but would not catch a subtly wrong-but-compiling\n358 |    argument.\n359 | 2. **Independent code review** — the full proof scripts (lines 78–153 for\n360 |    `integral`, lines 172–378 for `integralOperator_nonneg`) were read\n361 |    line-by-line and checked for logical soundness: the Fubini swap, the\n362 |    a.e.-non-negativity of the PD quadratic-form integrand, the Riemann-sum\n363 |    construction, the uniform-continuity error bound, and the final\n364 |    `Complex.nonneg_iff` split.  This confirms the *logic* is sound, not just\n365 |    that the kernel accepted it.\n366 | \n367 | These are complementary: a clean `#print axioms` alone would not have caught\n368 | a wrong-but-still-compiling argument, and a code review alone would not have\n369 | caught a silently-introduced axiom.  Both were done.\n370 | \n371 | **Mathlib-absence verification.** Both `PositiveDefinite.integral` and\n372 | `PositiveDefinite.integralOperator_nonneg` were checked against the current\n373 | Mathlib version (pinned in `lake-manifest.json`) and confirmed **absent** via\n374 | multiple independent search angles:\n375 | \n376 | - `PositiveDefinite` as a bare identifier does not exist anywhere in Mathlib\n377 |   (the matrix/quadratic-form positive-definiteness machinery Mathlib does have\n378 |   — `Matrix.PosDef`, `PosSemidef`, etc. — never touches Haar measure anywhere\n379 |   in the codebase; `grep` for the intersection returns zero files).\n380 | - Loogle search `IsCompact _ -> _ -> 0 ≤ _` over all 126 declarations\n381 |   mentioning both `IsCompact` and `LE.le` returns **no matches** — a genuine\n382 |   negative from the search index, not a grep miss.\n383 | - Loogle search `0 ≤ ∫ _, _ ∂_` returns 13 hits, every one of which is\n384 |   generic integral-nonnegativity from a pointwise-nonnegative integrand\n385 |   (`integral_nonneg`, `setIntegral_nonneg`, AE-equality lemmas).  Nothing\n386 |   group-theoretic, nothing kernel-based, nothing resembling \"PD kernel ⟹\n387 |   positive operator.\"\n388 | - Related concepts (Godement's theorem on positive-definite functions,\n389 |   Bochner theorem for groups, unitary-representation character machinery,\n390 |   convolution on compact groups) are likewise not present under those names.\n391 | \n392 | This is a multi-angle confirmation that these two lemmas are genuinely new to\n393 | Mathlib, not a rediscovery of existing infrastructure.  The framing is\n394 | therefore \"confirmed absent from Mathlib as of this Mathlib version,\" not\n395 | \"might be reusable Mathlib-adjacent infrastructure\" — a stronger, citable\n396 | claim if this work is ever upstreamed.\n397 | \n398 | **Key Mathlib API names verified against pinned version.** The proof of\n399 | `integralOperator_nonneg` depends on two non-trivial Mathlib lemmas whose\n400 | names were checked against the pinned Mathlib commit\n401 | (`3bc2a1801c2416549ba5ba0b3f5728a28b87e7d9`, Lean v4.33) to catch\n402 | toolchain-drift breakage proactively:\n403 | \n404 | - `measureReal_prod_prod` — confirmed present in\n405 |   `Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Prod.lean` (as\n406 |   `_root_.MeasureTheory.measureReal_prod_prod`).\n407 | - `finite_cover_balls_of_compact` — confirmed present in\n408 |   `Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/Pseudo/Basic.lean` (with alias\n409 |   `IsCompact.finite_cover_balls`).\n410 | \n411 | Both names match the current Mathlib; `lake build\n412 | YangMills.Proofs.PositiveDefiniteIntegral` succeeds with 0 errors.  This\n413 | file is **not** in the toolchain-drift-breakage risk category.\n414 | \n415 | ### Lattice action and reflection lemmas\n416 | - `reflectSite_involution`, `reflection_involution`\n417 | - `total_wilson_action_decomposition_z4` (S_W = S_W⁺ + S_W⁻ + S_W⁰)\n418 | - `neg_action_reflection_z4`, `interface_action_reflection_symmetric_z4`,\n419 |   `wilsonActionFiniteConfig_reflection_invariant`\n420 | - Periodic-site variants: `signedTime_neg`, `plaquette_classification`,\n421 |   `total_decomposition_os_periodic`, etc.\n422 | - `trace_plaquetteProduct_reflect_ss/_ts/_st/_tt`\n423 | - `neg_action_reflection_os_periodic`,\n424 |   `interface_action_reflection_symmetric_os_periodic`\n425 | \n426 | ### Measure theory\n427 | - `productHaarMeasure`, `IsProbabilityMeasure` instance\n428 | - `measurable_extendLinkVariable`, `measurable_wilsonActionFiniteConfig`\n429 | - `partitionFunctionFinite_pos` — **proved for both empty and nonempty\n430 |   sites** (earlier README versions incorrectly listed the nonempty case as\n431 |   a sorry — confirmed fixed, this entry corrects that)\n432 | - `gibbsExpectation_pos`, `gibbsExpectation_normalization`\n433 | - `gibbsExpectation_linear` — **proved, with integrability hypotheses\n434 |   added to the interface** (earlier README versions listed this as\n435 |   in-progress without hypotheses — confirmed this was resolved by adding\n436 |   the hypotheses, not by proving the false unconditional statement)\n437 | - `measurable_plaquetteContribution`,\n438 |   `measurable_wilsonActionOSPositive/Negative/Interface`\n439 | - `measure_factorization'` (μ₀ ≅ μ⁺ × μ⁻ × μ⁰, proved via `MeasurePreserving`)\n440 |   — verified by `#print axioms` (only `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound`),\n441 |   0 sorries, under the current Lean v4.33 toolchain.\n442 | - `haarMeasure_inv_invariant` (`LatticeMeasure.lean`) — the Haar measure on\n443 |   `SU(N)` is invariant under inversion `g ↦ g⁻¹`, i.e.\n444 |   `map Inv.inv (haarMeasure K) = haarMeasure K`.  **Proved** (0 sorries, 0\n445 |   custom axioms — verified by `#print axioms`: only `propext`,\n446 |   `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).  The proof uses the standard\n447 |   compact-group unimodularity argument: `haarMeasure K` is right-invariant\n448 |   (compact groups are unimodular — `map (· * g) μ` is left-invariant and a\n449 |   probability measure, so by `isMulInvariant_eq_smul_of_compactSpace` it\n450 |   equals `haarScalarFactor • μ` with the scalar forced to `1` by\n451 |   `μ univ = 1`), hence `μ.inv` is left-invariant\n452 |   (`inv.instIsMulLeftInvariant`), and again by uniqueness `μ.inv = μ` since\n453 |   both are probability measures.  This is a known Mathlib fact, not a new\n454 |   result; the formalization work was the namespace/identifier plumbing\n455 |   (`Measure.map` vs `Matrix.map` shadowing, `Measure.haarScalarFactor`,\n456 |   `Measure.isMulInvariant_eq_smul_of_compactSpace`) and avoiding the\n457 |   dependent-rewrite motive failure when evaluating the scalar smul at\n458 |   `Set.univ` (via `congr_arg (fun ν => ν Set.univ) h_eq`).\n459 | - `reflectLinkVariable_measurePreserving` (`LatticeMeasure.lean`) — the\n460 |   reflection map `θ` on the full link-variable group is measure-preserving\n461 |   w.r.t. the product Haar measure.  **Proved** (0 sorries, 0 custom axioms —\n462 |   verified by `#print axioms`: only `propext`, `Classical.choice`,\n463 |   `Quot.sound`).  The statement carries the necessary hypothesis\n464 |   `hsites : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → reflectSite n ∈ sites` (which, since\n465 |   `ReflectSite.involution` makes `reflectSite` involutive, makes the\n466 |   reflection a bijection on `sites`).  The proof composes two\n467 |   measure-preserving maps via `MeasurePreserving.comp`: (1) the index\n468 |   permutation `(n, μ) ↦ (reflectSite n, μ)` preserves the product measure\n469 |   by `measurePreserving_piCongrLeft` (all factors are identical); (2)\n470 |   componentwise inversion on time-like links (μ = 0) preserves the product\n471 |    measure by `measurePreserving_pi` + `haarMeasure_inv_invariant` (spatial\n472 |    links use `MeasurePreserving.id`).  This is the key measure-theoretic\n473 |    ingredient for the character-orthogonality approach to closing\n474 |    `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`.\n475 | - `reflectLinkVariable_measurePreserving_between` (`LatticeMeasure.lean`) —\n476 |   generalizes `reflectLinkVariable_measurePreserving` to the case where the\n477 |   source and target site sets **differ** (e.g. `negativeSites` →\n478 |   `positiveSites`), which is exactly what the change of variables\n479 |   `U⁻ ↦ V⁺ = reflect(U⁻)` in the transfer-matrix integral requires.\n480 |   **Proved** (0 sorries, 0 custom axioms — verified by `#print axioms`: only\n481 |   `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).  Same two-step composition\n482 |   (index bijection via `measurePreserving_piCongrLeft`, then componentwise\n483 |   inversion via `measurePreserving_pi` + `haarMeasure_inv_invariant`).\n484 | \n485 | ### Transfer matrix\n486 | - `reflectToPosInterface`, `transferMatrixCorrect`, `G`, `g_posInterface`\n487 |   (definitions)\n488 | - `reflectPosToNeg`, `reflectNegToPos`, `sigmaInterface` (definitions) — the\n489 |   change-of-variables map `U⁻ ↦ V⁺ = reflect(U⁻)` (`reflectNegToPos`), its\n490 |   inverse `V⁺ ↦ U⁻ = reflect(V⁺)` (`reflectPosToNeg`), and the σ reflection on\n491 |   interface configs (inverts time-like links, keeps spatial).\n492 | - `reflectToPosInterface_involution` (`TransferMatrix.lean`) — the key\n493 |   involution property for the change of variables in step (b) of the\n494 |   `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` closure plan:\n495 |   `reflectToPosInterface(reflectPosToNeg(V⁺), u⁰) = mergePosInterface(V⁺, σ(u⁰))`.\n496 |   **Proved** (0 sorries, 0 custom axioms — verified by `#print axioms`: only\n497 |   `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n498 | - `reflectPosToNeg_reflectNegToPos` (`TransferMatrix.lean`) — `reflectPosToNeg`\n499 |   is the left-inverse of `reflectNegToPos` (reflecting a negative config to\n500 |   positive and back recovers the original, via `reflection_involution`).\n501 |   **Proved** (0 sorries, 0 custom axioms).\n502 | - `restrictLinkVariable_negative_extendToFullConfig`,\n503 |   `restrictPosInterface_extendToFullConfig`,\n504 |   `reflect_extendToFullConfig_posInterface` (`TransferMatrix.lean`) — supporting\n505 |   lemmas for the change of variables: restricting `extendToFullConfig` recovers\n506 |   the components, and the positive+interface restriction of the reflected full\n507 |   config `reflectLinkVariable(extendToFullConfig(reflectPosToNeg V⁺, u))` equals\n508 |   `mergePosInterface V⁺ (σ(restrictToInterface u))`. **Proved** (0 sorries, 0\n509 |   custom axioms).\n510 | - `transferMatrix_integrand_change_of_variables` (`TransferMatrix.lean`) — the\n511 |   **pointwise identity** underlying the change of variables: the transfer-matrix\n512 |   integrand at `U⁻` equals the transformed integrand at\n513 |   `V⁺ = reflectNegToPos(U⁻)`, rewriting `ψ(θ⁻⁰(U⁻, u⁰))` → `ψ(V⁺, σ(u⁰))` and\n514 |   `S⁻(U⁻)` → `S⁺(V⁺, σ(u⁰))` via `neg_action_reflection_os_periodic` and\n515 |   `reflectToPosInterface_involution`. **Proved** (0 sorries, 0 custom axioms —\n516 |   verified by `#print axioms`: only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n517 | - `transferMatrixReflected` (`TransferMatrix.lean`) — the transfer matrix after\n518 |   the change of variables `U⁻ ↦ V⁺ = reflect(U⁻)`, where the negative-time\n519 |   integral has been replaced by a positive-time integral.\n520 | - `transferMatrix_change_of_variables` (`TransferMatrix.lean`) — the\n521 |   **integral-level change of variables** (sub-step 2 of step (b)): shows\n522 |   `transferMatrixCorrect = transferMatrixReflected` by applying\n523 |   `reflectLinkVariable_measurePreserving_between` (measure-preserving from μ⁻\n524 |   to μ⁺) via `integral_map` together with the pointwise identity\n525 |   `transferMatrix_integrand_change_of_variables`. **Proved** (0 sorries, 0 custom\n526 |   axioms — verified by `#print axioms`: only `propext`, `Classical.choice`,\n527 |   `Quot.sound`). **This completes step (b) of the closure plan.**\n528 | - `signedTime_reflectSite`, `reflectSite_mem_negative_of_positive`,\n529 |   `reflectSite_mem_positive_of_negative`, `reflectSite_mem_interface_of_interface`,\n530 |   `reflectSite_not_mem_*` (`ReflectionPositivity.lean`) — helper lemmas\n531 |   characterizing how `reflectSite` maps between the positive/negative/interface\n532 |   site sets. **Proved** (0 sorries, 0 custom axioms).\n533 | - `G_thetaG_factorization_clean`, `G_thetaG_factorization`\n534 | - `osG_thetaG_factorization` (`ReflectionPositivity.lean`) — the clean\n535 |   algebraic identity `osG(U)·osG(θU) = f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β S_W(U))`,\n536 |   showing `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` is equivalent to\n537 |   `∫ f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β S_W) dμ ≥ 0`.  0 sorries, 0 axioms.\n538 | - `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` — the key identity linking the\n539 |   reflected Gibbs expectation to the transfer-matrix inner product;\n540 |   verified by `#print axioms` (only `propext, Classical.choice,\n541 |   Quot.sound`), 0 sorries, under the current Lean v4.33 toolchain.\n542 | - `measurable_G`, `integrand_measurable`, `measurable_reflectLinkVariable`\n543 | - `measure_factorization'` in `TransferMatrix.lean` —\n544 |   measure-preserving equivalence between the full lattice measure and the\n545 |   positive/negative/interface factorization. Verified by `#print axioms`\n546 |   (only `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound`), 0 sorries, under the\n547 |   current Lean v4.33 toolchain.\n548 | \n549 | ## Known incomplete / incorrect items\n550 | \n551 | 1. **Vacuous proof (`hadd` issue).** `gibbsExpectationZ4_reflection_positive`\n552 |    for the nonempty finite-lattice case only goes through because the\n553 |    `hadd` hypothesis (closure under forward time translation) forces\n554 |    `sites = ∅` on a finite lattice, making the \"proof\" true by\n555 |    contradiction rather than by establishing the actual inequality. **This\n556 |    is not a real theorem for any nonempty lattice.** Fix options: switch\n557 |    to periodic boundary conditions so `hadd` is satisfiable on a nonempty\n558 |    finite lattice, prove the nonempty case directly without `hadd`, or move\n559 |    to an infinite lattice. Until fixed, do not cite this lemma as\n560 |    establishing reflection positivity for any actual configuration.\n561 | \n562 | 2. **Periodic-lattice reflection positivity is unresolved — status now\n563 |    confirmed precisely.** `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive`\n564 |    closes via `exact transferMatrixPositivity_axiom ...`, a genuine `axiom`\n565 |    declared in `ReflectionPositivity.lean` (not a `sorry`, and not in\n566 |    `TransferMatrix.lean`). All of the algebraic and measure-theoretic\n567 |    bookkeeping around it — including `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg`,\n568 |    `measure_factorization'`, and the clean factorization\n569 |    `osG_thetaG_factorization` — is fully proved; the axiom is the only gap.\n570 |    The clean factorization shows the axiom is equivalent to\n571 |    `∫ f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β S_W) dμ ≥ 0`, and `boltzmannFactorPD` proves the\n572 |    Boltzmann factor `exp(-β S_W)` is PD on the full link group (modulo\n573 |    Peter–Weyl).  **However**, this integral is NOT the standard PD quadratic\n574 |    form that `integralOperator_nonneg` addresses — it is a single integral\n575 |    with the geometric reflection `θ` and `K` evaluated at `g` (not `g⁻¹h`).\n576 |    PD-ness of `K` does not imply non-negativity; the Peter–Weyl character\n577 |    expansion + the newly added `characterOrthogonality` axiom (Schur\n578 |    orthogonality) are needed to decompose the integrand into\n579 |    `|Fourier coefficients|²`.  See the \"character-orthogonality path\" above.\n580 | \n581 | 3. **Systematic audit for vacuous proofs not yet done.** The `hadd` pattern\n582 |    (item 1) is a known instance of a broader risk: any proof that goes\n583 |    through via deriving a false/unsatisfiable hypothesis rather than\n584 |    proving the stated claim. A full pass checking every top-level theorem\n585 |    (e.g. via `#print axioms` plus manual inspection for\n586 |    contradiction-derivation patterns) has not yet been completed.\n587 | \n588 | 4. **Repo hygiene (addressed).** The empty `Coq/` and `Z3/`\n589 |    placeholder directories and the stale `TransferMatrix_FIXED.lean.lf` /\n590 |    `TransferMatrix.lean.lf` intermediate-version files have been removed\n591 |    (they remain recoverable from git history). `TransferMatrix.lean` has\n592 |    unusual whitespace suggesting post-processing artifacts.\n593 |    `proofs/attempts.jsonl` is raw AI proof-attempt log output and is\n594 |    retained as a record of verification attempts; it is not part of the\n595 |    build.\n596 | \n597 | 5. **`Overview.lean` was stale (fixed).** It previously undersold:\n598 |    it claimed `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` \"is not yet formalized\" (false —\n599 |    it's proved, verified by `#print axioms`) and referenced a\n600 |    `transferMatrixCorrect_positive` lemma \"currently sorry\" that does not exist\n601 |    under that name (the real gap is the differently-named\n602 |    `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom` axiom, in `ReflectionPositivity.lean`).\n603 |    Both documents are now updated to match the source; the\n604 |    same continuous-maintenance discipline applies going forward.\n605 | \n606 | 6. **`TransferMatrix.lean` toolchain-drift build break — FIXED.** The\n607 |    repo's `lean-toolchain` was `v4.32.0-rc1` but `lake-manifest.json` pins\n608 |    a Mathlib commit requiring `v4.33.0-rc1`; `lake build` auto-bumps the\n609 |    toolchain and rebuilds.  Several `simp`-based proofs in\n610 |    `TransferMatrix.lean` (subtype-coercion goals in `measure_factorization'`\n611 |    and the bijectivity/equiv lemmas) no longer closed under the new `simp`\n612 |    normal form.  This was **toolchain drift**, not a logical error.  All\n613 |    break sites have been fixed this session; `TransferMatrix.lean` now\n614 |    builds cleanly under v4.33, and `#print axioms` on\n615 |    `measure_factorization'` and `integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg` confirms\n616 |    they depend only on `propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound` (no custom\n617 |    axiom, 0 sorries).  The full `lake build` succeeds.\n618 | \n619 | ## Project structure\n620 | \n621 | ```\n622 | YangMills/\n623 | ├── src/\n624 | │   ├── lean/\n625 | │   │   ├── YangMills.lean\n626 | │   │   └── YangMills/\n627 | │   │       ├── Overview.lean\n628 | │   │       ├── SpecialUnitary.lean\n629 | │   │       ├── OSAxioms.lean\n630 | │   │       ├── GaugeTheory.lean\n631 | │   │       ├── Lattice.lean\n632 | │   │       ├── MassGap.lean\n633 | │   │       ├── ContinuumLimit.lean      # invokes continuum_limit_exists\n634 | │   │       ├── MassGapProof.lean        # invokes mass_gap_axiom — see status warning above\n635 | │   │       └── Proofs/\n636 | │   │           ├── BasicLemmas.lean\n637 | │   │           ├── GaugeInvariance.lean\n638 | │   │           ├── JacobiIdentity.lean\n639 | │   │           ├── LatticeMeasure.lean\n640 | │   │           ├── PeterWeyl.lean               # Peter–Weyl axiom, plaquetteBoltzmannPD(_inv)\n641 | │   │           ├── PositiveDefinite.lean       # PD function algebra (add, mul, prod, finprod, …)\n642 | │   │           ├── PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean  # PD.integral, integralOperator_nonneg, Mercer-PD kernels\n643 | │   │           ├── BoltzmannFactor.lean        # boltzmannFactorPD (full Boltzmann factor is PD)\n644 | │   │           ├── ReflectionPositivity.lean   # transferMatrixPositivity_axiom, osG_thetaG_factorization\n645 | │   │           ├── TransferMatrix.lean         # transferMatrixCorrect, integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg\n646 | │   │           └── MassGapProof.lean\n647 | ├── proofs/                             # attempts.jsonl — raw AI proof-attempt log, not part of build\n648 | ├── verify/                             # verification scripts (lean.bat, coq.bat, z3.bat, …)\n649 | ├── docs/\n650 | ├── literature/\n651 | ├── lakefile.lean\n652 | ├── lean-toolchain\n653 | └── README.md\n654 | ```\n655 | \n656 | ## Building\n657 | \n658 | ```bash\n659 | curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/leanprover/elan/master/elan-init.sh | sh\n660 | cd YangMills\n661 | lake build\n662 | ```\n663 | \n664 | To check what a given theorem actually depends on:\n665 | \n666 | ```\n667 | #print axioms YourTheoremName\n668 | ```\n669 | \n670 | Run this on every top-level theorem before describing it as proved.\n671 | \n672 | ## Key design decisions\n673 | \n674 | - Euclidean formulation via Osterwalder–Schrader axioms rather than\n675 |   Minkowski Wightman axioms directly, to use reflection positivity and\n676 |   stochastic methods.\n677 | - Lattice discretization as a bridge between finite approximations and\n678 |   continuum QFT (Wilson's lattice gauge theory).\n679 | - Four-corner plaquette classification for the Wilson action decomposition,\n680 |   to make the reflection symmetry identities hold.\n681 | - `SU(N)` for general N ≥ 2 via Mathlib's `Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup`.\n682 | \n683 | ## Keeping this README (and `Overview.lean`) honest\n684 | \n685 | Documentation drift in this project is not a one-time bug, it's a recurring\n686 | pattern, and it goes in **both directions**: this README has previously\n687 | reported sorries as open that had been closed, and reported lemmas as\n688 | complete without noting the axioms they secretly depended on;\n689 | `Overview.lean` previously reported a fully-proved\n690 | lemma (`integral_G_thetaG_eq_inner_g_Tg`) as unformalized and referenced a\n691 | `sorry`'d lemma by a name that doesn't match anything in the actual\n692 | codebase (both now fixed). Treat both documents as equally prone to drift\n693 | and equally in need of upkeep:\n694 | \n695 | - Every session that changes proof state must update the \"What is actually\n696 |   proved\" / \"Known incomplete\" sections of this README **and** the\n697 |   corresponding status notes in `Overview.lean`, in the same session, not\n698 |   later.\n699 | - Never describe a theorem as proved without having run\n700 |   `#print axioms` on it in that session.\n701 | - Never describe the top-level Millennium Prize theorem as proved, nearly\n702 |   proved, or as making progress, while `mass_gap_axiom` (or anything\n703 |   equivalent to the conjecture) remains in its dependency tree.\n704 | - When a module docstring (e.g. `MassGapProof.lean`'s \"the proof uses four\n705 |   axioms\") states a count or fact about the codebase, verify that count\n706 |   against the actual source in the same session — the axiom count there is\n707 |   currently wrong (says four, lists five; the actual count is now six with\n708 |   the addition of `characterOrthogonality`).\n709 | - If a claim in this README or `Overview.lean` can't be verified against\n710 |   current source in under a few minutes, mark it `[UNVERIFIED — recheck]`\n711 |   rather than leaving a confident-sounding but possibly stale statement in\n712 |   place.\n713 | \n714 | ## Mathlib candidate packaging\n715 | \n716 | Three general-purpose results (Mercer-type positive-definite kernels and two\n717 | group-theoretic PD lemmas) have been extracted into standalone,\n718 | Yang-Mills-free files for independent review by Mathlib maintainers. They\n719 | are pure group/measure/kernel theory, verified by `#print axioms` to depend\n720 | only on `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` (0 `sorry`, 0 custom\n721 | axiom). See **`MATHLIB_SUBMISSION.md`** at the repo root for the full\n722 | summary, absence-verification report, and reproduction steps. The standalone\n723 | files are:\n724 | \n725 | - `PositiveDefiniteKernelMathlibCandidate.lean` (repo root) — **priority\n726 |   candidate**: Mercer-type PD kernels (no group structure), including\n727 |   `PositiveDefiniteKernel.integralOperator_nonneg` and the full building-block\n728 |   suite (`.conj_symm`, `.one`, `.mul`, `.smul_nonneg`, `.finprod`, `.comp`,\n729 |   `.continuous_comp`, `.sum_nonneg_of_map`, `toPositiveDefiniteKernel`).\n730 | - `PositiveDefiniteMathlibCandidate.lean` (repo root) — group-theoretic PD\n731 |   functions: `PositiveDefinite.integral` and\n732 |   `PositiveDefinite.integralOperator_nonneg`.\n733 | \n734 | A search of external repositories found `Vilin97/lean-pool` contains\n735 | `IsPositiveDefinite` (same group-PD concept, different API), which is noted\n736 | for reviewer awareness in `MATHLIB_SUBMISSION.md`. The Mercer-type\n737 | `PositiveDefiniteKernel` has no known duplicate anywhere checked.\n738 | \n739 | These results are unrelated to the (unsolved) Yang-Mills mass-gap difficulty\n740 | and are offered as standalone infrastructure.\n741 | \n742 | ## References\n743 | \n744 | See `literature/survey.md` and `docs/strategy.md`.\n745 | \n746 | ## License\n747 | \n748 | Academic use. No warranty.\n","timestamp":1785482741,"token_count":16377,"tool_call_id":"d0cf5f6a-4450-43a2-a8b0-8e6f43ff3a03","full_token_estimate":10659,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"README.md","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":748,"byte_count":49206,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":25,"edit_line":null},"turn":1,"is_prune_marker":false}
