{"id":37,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PositiveDefinite.lean\n-- 830 lines, 40164 bytes --\n800 |     (∀ g : G, ∀ v ∈ W, ρ g *ᵥ v ∈ W) → (W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤)\n801 | \n802 | /-- **Axiom (Schur orthogonality for characters of irreducible unitary\n803 | representations of a compact group).**\n804 | \n805 | For a compact group `G` with normalized Haar measure `μ`, and irreducible\n806 | unitary representations `ρ_λ, ρ_μ` with characters `χ_λ, χ_μ`, the integral\n807 | `∫ χ_λ(g) · conj(χ_μ(g)) dμ(g)` equals `1` if `λ = μ` (the same irrep) and\n808 | `0` otherwise (distinct irreps).\n809 | \n810 | This is the **Great Orthogonality Theorem** for compact groups (Schur\n811 | orthogonality), a cornerstone of the Peter–Weyl theorem.  It is not currently\n812 | in Mathlib.  The axiom is stated for a *finite* index set of irreps (the\n813 | Peter–Weyl theorem gives a countable family; for the lattice Boltzmann factor\n814 | only finitely many irreps appear in the character expansion, so a finite\n815 | family suffices).\n816 | \n817 | See `docs/gap_analysis.md` for how this axiom is used to close the\n818 | reflection-positivity gap. -/\n819 | axiom characterOrthogonality {G : Type*} [Group G] [TopologicalSpace G]\n820 |     [CompactSpace G] [MeasurableSpace G] [BorelSpace G]\n821 |     (μ : Measure G) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]\n822 |     (ι : Type) [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (dims : ι → ℕ)\n823 |     (ρ : ∀ i, G →* Matrix (Fin (dims i)) (Fin (dims i)) ℂ)\n824 |     (hU : ∀ i, IsUnitaryRepresentation (ρ i))\n825 |     (hIrr : ∀ i, IsIrreducible (ρ i))\n826 |     (i j : ι) :\n827 |     ∫ g, repCharacter (ρ i) g * conj (repCharacter (ρ j) g) ∂μ =\n828 |       if i = j then (1 : ℂ) else 0\n829 | \n830 | end UnitaryRepresentation\n","timestamp":1785484621,"token_count":539,"tool_call_id":"92ff0df9-b34a-4717-a444-3cb70b1bef44","full_token_estimate":371,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/PositiveDefin