{"id":38,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean\n-- 1165 lines, 59221 bytes --\n 985 | The following abstract lemma is the pure measure-theory scaffold for the\n 986 | character-orthogonality approach to closing `transferMatrixPositivity_axiom`.\n 987 | It uses no group structure and no character orthogonality — only the\n 988 | measure-preserving change of variables and the fact that `f` is real-valued\n 989 | (so `conj (f x) = (f x : ℂ)`).\n 990 | \n 991 | If a kernel `K : X → Y → ℂ` has a finite separable decomposition\n 992 | `K(x, y) = ∑_i a_i · Φ_i(x) · conj(Φ_i(θ y))` with `a_i ≥ 0` and `θ`\n 993 | measure-preserving (`θ_*ν = μ`), then for real-valued `f`:\n 994 | `∫∫ f(x) · f(θ y) · K(x, y) dν(y) dμ(x) = ∑_i a_i · ‖∫ f · Φ_i dμ‖² ≥ 0`.\n 995 | \n 996 | This is the abstract scaffold that the concrete Peter–Weyl character expansion\n 997 | of the transfer-matrix kernel would plug into.  See `docs/gap_analysis.md` for\n 998 | the full analysis of the remaining wiring (which requires the Clebsch–Gordan\n 999 | decomposition for products of characters of the same link variable). -/\n1000 | \n1001 | /-- **Character-expansion positivity (abstract lemma).**  If a kernel\n1002 | `K : X → Y → ℂ` has a finite separable decomposition\n1003 | `K(x, y) = ∑_i a_i · Φ_i(x) · conj(Φ_i(θ y))` with `a_i ≥ 0` and `θ`\n1004 | measure-preserving (`θ_*ν = μ`), then for real-valued `f`:\n1005 | `∫∫ f(x) · f(θ y) · K(x, y) dν(y) dμ(x) = ∑_i a_i · ‖∫ f · Φ_i dμ‖²`.\n1006 | \n1007 | No group structure, no character orthogonality — only the measure-preserving\n1008 | change of variables and the fact that `f` is real-valued. -/\n1009 | lemma character_expansion_positivity\n1010 |     {X Y : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] [MeasurableSpace Y]\n1011 |     (μ : Measure X) (ν : Measure Y) [SigmaFinite μ] [SigmaFinite ν]\n1012 |     (θ : Y → X) (hθ : MeasurePreserving θ ν μ)\n1013 |     (ι : Type*) [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n1014 |     (a : ι → ℝ)\n1015 |     (Φ : ι → X → ℂ) (f : X → ℝ)\n1016 |     (hΦ_meas : ∀ i, AEStronglyMeasurable (Φ i) μ)\n1017 |     (hf_meas : AEStronglyMeasurable (fun x => (f x : ℂ)) μ)\n1018 |     (hfΦ_int : ∀ i, Integrable (fun x => (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) μ)\n1019 |     (K : X → Y → ℂ)\n1020 |     (hK : ∀ x y, K x y = ∑ i, (a i : ℂ) * (Φ i x * conj (Φ i (θ y)))) :\n1021 |     ∫ x, ∫ y, (f x : ℂ) * (f (θ y) : ℂ) * K x y ∂ν ∂μ =\n1022 |       ↑(∑ i, a i * ‖∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ‖^2) := by\n1023 |   -- Helper: AEStronglyMeasurable of conj(Φ i)\n1024 |   have hΦ_conj_meas : ∀ i, AEStronglyMeasurable (fun x => conj (Φ i x)) μ :=\n1025 |     fun i => Complex.continuous_conj.comp_aestronglyMeasurable (hΦ_meas i)\n1026 |   -- Helper: AEStronglyMeasurable of (f * conj(Φ i))\n1027 |   have hfΦ_conj_meas : ∀ i, AEStronglyMeasurable (fun x => (f x : ℂ) * conj (Φ i x)) μ :=\n1028 |     fun i => hf_meas.mul (hΦ_conj_meas i)\n1029 |   -- Helper: Integrable of (f * conj(Φ i)) — derived from hfΦ_int via norm equality\n1030 |   have hfΦ_conj_int : ∀ i, Integrable (fun x => (f x : ℂ) * conj (Φ i x)) μ := by\n1031 |     intro i\n1032 |     refine ⟨hfΦ_conj_meas i, ?_⟩\n1033 |     have hnorm : ∀ x, ‖(f x : ℂ) * conj (Φ i x)‖ = ‖(f x : ℂ) * Φ i x‖ := fun x => by\n1034 |       rw [norm_mul, norm_mul, Complex.norm_conj]\n1035 |     have hfi := (hfΦ_int i).2\n1036 |     rw [hasFiniteIntegral_iff_norm] at hfi ⊢\n1037 |     rw [lintegral_congr_ae (ae_of_all μ (fun x => by rw [hnorm]))]\n1038 |     exact hfi\n1039 |   -- Helper: Integrable of (f(θy) * conj(Φ i (θy))) w.r.t. ν\n1040 |   have hfΦ_conj_θ_int : ∀ i, Integrable (fun y => (f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y))) ν :=\n1041 |     fun i => hθ.integrable_comp (hfΦ_conj_meas i) |>.mpr (hfΦ_conj_int i)\n1042 |   -- Helper: change of variables ∫_ν f(θy)·conj(Φ_i(θy)) dy = ∫_μ f(x)·conj(Φ_i(x)) dx\n1043 |   have hchange_var : ∀ i,\n1044 |       ∫ y, (f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y)) ∂ν = ∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * conj (Φ i x) ∂μ := by\n1045 |     intro i\n1046 |     have hfm := hfΦ_conj_meas i\n1047 |     rw [← hθ.map_eq] at hfm ⊢\n1048 |     exact (integral_map hθ.measurable.aemeasurable hfm).symm\n1049 |   -- Helper: ∫_μ f·conj(Φ_i) = conj(∫_μ f·Φ_i)  (since f is real-valued)\n1050 |   have hconj_int : ∀ i,\n1051 |       ∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * conj (Φ i x) ∂μ = conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ) := by\n1052 |     intro i\n1053 |     have heq : ∀ x, (f x : ℂ) * conj (Φ i x) = conj ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) := by\n1054 |       intro x\n1055 |       symm\n1056 |       rw [map_mul (starRingEnd ℂ), Complex.conj_ofReal]\n1057 |     rw [show (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * conj (Φ i x) ∂μ) =\n1058 |         ∫ x, conj ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) ∂μ from by congr 1 with x; exact heq x]\n1059 |     exact Complex.conjCLE.integral_comp_comm _\n1060 |   -- Main computation\n1061 |   -- Substitute hK into the integrand\n1062 |   have hK_subst : ∀ x y,\n1063 |       (f x : ℂ) * (f (θ y) : ℂ) * K x y =\n1064 |         ∑ i, (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) * ((f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y))) := by\n1065 |     intro x y\n1066 |     rw [hK, Finset.mul_sum]\n1067 |     apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n1068 |     intro i _\n1069 |     ring\n1070 |   -- Integrability of the inner-integral function (for fixed x, each i)\n1071 |   have hinner_int : ∀ (x : X) (i : ι),\n1072 |       Integrable (fun y => (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1073 |         ((f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y)))) ν := by\n1074 |     intro x i\n1075 |     have h := (hfΦ_conj_θ_int i).mul_const ((a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x))\n1076 |     have heq_fun : (fun y => (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1077 |         ((f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y)))) =\n1078 |         (fun y => ((f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y))) *\n1079 |           ((a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x))) := by\n1080 |       funext y; ring\n1081 |     rw [heq_fun]; exact h\n1082 |   -- Step 1: rewrite the LHS using hK_subst\n1083 |   rw [show (∫ x, ∫ y, (f x : ℂ) * (f (θ y) : ℂ) * K x y ∂ν ∂μ) =\n1084 |         ∫ x, ∫ y, ∑ i, (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1085 |           ((f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y))) ∂ν ∂μ from by\n1086 |     congr 1 with x\n1087 |     congr 1 with y\n1088 |     exact hK_subst x y]\n1089 |   -- Step 2: exchange the sum with the inner integral (over y)\n1090 |   rw [show (∫ x, ∫ y, ∑ i, (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1091 |         ((f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y))) ∂ν ∂μ) =\n1092 |       ∫ x, ∑ i, (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1093 |         ∫ y, (f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y)) ∂ν ∂μ from by\n1094 |     congr 1 with x\n1095 |     rw [integral_finsetSum Finset.univ (fun i _ => hinner_int x i)]\n1096 |     apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n1097 |     intro i _\n1098 |     rw [show (fun y => (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1099 |         ((f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y)))) =\n1100 |         (fun y => ((a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x)) •\n1101 |           ((f (θ y) : ℂ) * conj (Φ i (θ y)))) from by\n1102 |       funext y; rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_assoc]]\n1103 |     rw [integral_smul, smul_eq_mul, mul_assoc]]\n1104 |   -- Step 3: apply change of variables to the inner integral\n1105 |   simp only [hchange_var]\n1106 |   -- Step 4: apply conj integral\n1107 |   simp only [hconj_int]\n1108 |   -- Step 5: exchange the sum with the outer integral (over x)\n1109 |   have houter_int : ∀ i, Integrable (fun x => (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1110 |       conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ)) μ := by\n1111 |     intro i\n1112 |     have h := (hfΦ_int i).mul_const ((a i : ℂ) * conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ))\n1113 |     have heq_fun : (fun x => (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1114 |         conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ)) =\n1115 |         (fun x => ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1116 |           ((a i : ℂ) * conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ))) := by\n1117 |       funext x; ring\n1118 |     rw [heq_fun]; exact h\n1119 |   rw [show (∫ x, ∑ i, (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1120 |         conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ) ∂μ) =\n1121 |       ∑ i, ∫ x, (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1122 |         conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ) ∂μ from by\n1123 |     rw [integral_finsetSum Finset.univ (fun i _ => houter_int i)]]\n1124 |   -- Step 6: convert RHS ↑(∑ i, a i * ‖...‖^2) to ∑ i, ↑(a i * ‖...‖^2)\n1125 |   rw [Complex.ofReal_sum]\n1126 |   -- Step 7: match term-by-term\n1127 |   apply Finset.sum_congr rfl\n1128 |   intro i _\n1129 |   rw [show (fun x => (a i : ℂ) * ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x) *\n1130 |         conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ)) =\n1131 |       (fun x => ((a i : ℂ) * conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ)) •\n1132 |         ((f x : ℂ) * Φ i x)) from by\n1133 |     funext x; rw [smul_eq_mul]; ring]\n1134 |   rw [integral_smul, smul_eq_mul]\n1135 |   -- Step 8: rearrange to conj(z) * z = normSq z = ‖z‖^2 and coerce\n1136 |   rw [show ((a i : ℂ) * conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ) *\n1137 |         ∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ) =\n1138 |       (a i : ℂ) * (conj (∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ) *\n1139 |         ∫ x, (f x : ℂ) * Φ i x ∂μ) from by ring]\n1140 |   rw [← Complex.normSq_eq_conj_mul_self, Complex.normSq_eq_norm_sq, Complex.ofReal_mul]\n1141 | \n1142 | /-- **Corollary: the character-expansion integral is non-negative.**  Under the\n1143 | same hypotheses as `character_expansion_positivity` (in particular `a i ≥ 0`),\n1144 | the integral `∫∫ f(x)·f(θ y)·K(x, y) dν dμ` is non-negative, since it equals a\n1145 | sum of non-negative weights `a i` times squared norms `‖∫ f·Φ_i‖²`. -/\n1146 | lemma character_expansion_nonneg\n1147 |     {X Y : Type*} [MeasurableSpace X] [MeasurableSpace Y]\n1148 |     (μ : Measure X) (ν : Measure Y) [SigmaFinite μ] [SigmaFinite ν]\n1149 |     (θ : Y → X) (hθ : MeasurePreserving θ ν μ)\n1150 |     (ι : Type*) [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]\n1151 |     (a : ι → ℝ) (ha : ∀ i, 0 ≤ a i)\n1152 |     (Φ : ι → X → ℂ) (f : X → ℝ)\n1153 |     (hΦ_meas : ∀ i, AEStronglyMeasurable (Φ i) μ)\n1154 |     (hf_meas : AEStronglyMeasurable (fun x => (f x : ℂ)) μ)\n\n... 11 more line(s) below (use offset=1155 to continue reading)","timestamp":178548