{"id":49,"role":"Tool","content":"Search results (5):\n\n1. [https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-113/issue-3/General-proof-of-Osterwalder-Schrader-positivity-for-the-Wilson-action/cmp/1104160284.pdf]\n   PDF General Proof of Osterwalder-Schrader Positivity for the Wilson Action\n   Luscher [3] and independently Osterwalder and Seiler [4] have addressed the problem in two different ways. Luscher starting from the Wilson action builds up a Hubert space as a Fock space derived from equal time fields and explicitly constructs a transfer matrix [5] which he proves to be positive definite, in this context Osterwalder-Schrader positivity is proved for gauge invariant operators ...\n\n2. [https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF01221251]\n   General proof of Osterwalder-Schrader positivity for the Wilson action ...\n   We extend the proof by Osterwalder and Seiler of reflection positivity of lattice gauge theories with fermions to the case in which the reflection is performed with respect to planes containing sites. Our proof applies to all observables and relies on the particular structure of the Wilson action. This assures the positivity of the correlation functions 〈θ(F)F〉 for any gauge invariant ...\n\n3. [https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1987CMaPh.113..369M/abstract]\n   General proof of Osterwalder-Schrader positivity for the Wilson action ...\n   We extend the proof by Osterwalder and Seiler of reflection positivity of lattice gauge theories with fermions to the case in which the reflection is performed with respect to planes containing sites. Our proof applies to all observables and relies on the particular structure of the Wilson action. This assures the positivity of the correlation functions &lt;θ(F)F&gt; for any gauge invariant ...\n\n4. [https://rd.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/BF01221251.pdf]\n   PDF General proof of Osterwalder-Schrader positivity for the Wilson action\n   Lfischer sta from ting the Wilson builds action up a Hilbert space as a Fock space derived from time fields equal and explicitly constructs a transfer matrix [-5] which proves heto be positive definite. In this context Osterwalder-Schrader positivity is proved for gauge invariant operators constructed from the fields belonging togiven time slices.\n\n5. [https://inspirehep.net/literature/251466]\n   Osterwalder-schrader Positivity for the Wilson Action\n   Osterwalder-Seiler's proof of reflection positivity of lattice gauge theories with fermions is extended to the case in which the reflection is performed with respect to planes containing sites. Our proof applies to all observables and relies on the particular structure of the Wiklson action.\n\n","timestamp":1785485747,"token_count":670,"tool_call_id":"8f58d0c4-1936-423c-8963-7c6c2bec1729","full_token_estimate":563,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"web_search","file_path":null,"old_text":"Luscher 1987 \"Osterwalder-Schrader positivity\" Wilson action transfer matrix positivity proof character expansion lattice gauge theory","new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":null,"byte_count":2673,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":1167,"edit_line":null},"turn":30,"is_prune_marker":false}
