_decomp`)\n4. `PositiveDefinite.lean:819-828` (`characterOrthogonality` axiom statement)\n5. `PositiveDefiniteIntegral.lean:1009-1141` (`character_expansion_positivity` — the abstract scaffold, for the measure-theory techniques even though it doesn't apply directly)\n\nThe most likely path: define an operator B from the separable decomposition, show the reflected transfer matrix kernel equals B*·B's kernel, then ⟨g,Tg⟩=‖Bg‖²≥0. This is substantial formalization work. Consider the \"derived axiom\" intermediate approach (design doc §5): axiomatize the separable decomposition as a consequence of Peter-Weyl, prove positivity from it (pure measure theory + character orthogonality, removes transferMatrixPositivity_axiom → count stays 6), then prove the derived axiom from peterWeyl_clebschGordan_plaquette (count → 5). This decomposes the problem into cleaner pieces.\n\n## Conventions to follow\n\n- Every proof must be verified with `#print axioms` (only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound allowed — no custom axioms, no sorry).\n- Update README.md \"What is actually proved\" / \"Known incomplete\" sections AND Overview.lean in the SAME session as any proof-state change.\n- Never describe the top-level Millennium Prize theorem as proved while mass_gap_axiom remains.\n- Keep `lake build` clean after every step. Build with: `lake build > tmp_build_full.log 2>&1` then check `findstr /I \"error sorry Build completed\" tmp_build_full.log`.\n- The README has a \"Keeping this README honest\" section — follow its discipline.\n\n## Session management\n\nCall `name_session` first. Check `project_task_list` (item 9 \"Close transferMatrixPositivity_axiom...\" is in_progress and tracks steps c,d). Use `todo_list` for this session's concrete steps. Update project_task_list when step (c) or (d) completes. Hand off before context exhausts (~75%).","timestamp":1785487250,"token_count":2422,"tool_call_id":"afaf7fd4-f241-47a8-88d4-6709e8639b7c","full_token_estimate":1584,"tool_meta":{"tool_